# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded cube root of BF16
#
# cbrt(2^e m) = cbrt(2^e) cbrt(m): the cube root of the exponent part and of the 128 mantissas in [1, 2) are both
# tabulated as B32 values whose product rounds correctly to BF16, and subnormals have a table of their own. The
# exact cubes 0x1.bp+1 * 8^k are returned exactly. Round to nearest only: negative values give negative roots, +-0
# and +-inf map to themselves, NaN comes back quiet.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binaryb16/cbrt/cbrt_bf16.c.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/System/Numerics/BF16

